<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Coahuila</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Coahuila is a state of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a> bordering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas">Texas</a>, with its capital at Saltillo. Under Spanish rule it was a frontier province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a> exposed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apache">Apache</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comanche">Comanche</a> raids, and from 1824 it was joined with Texas as the Mexican state of Coahuila y Tejas until the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/texas-revolution">Texas Revolution</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venustiano-carranza">Venustiano Carranza</a>, leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexican-revolution">Mexican Revolution</a>, came from Coahuila.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/coahuila.jpg" alt="Coahuila" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: BlatZzz · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Espiga_de_trigo.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
